1
00:00:00,385 --> 00:00:03,775
A helpful answer is only part of an agent's job.

2
00:00:04,054 --> 00:00:06,979
Customers also need the right business action.

3
00:00:07,490 --> 00:00:12,889
In this walkthrough, we will explain four agents, their tools and flows,
then

4
00:00:12,970 --> 00:00:18,206
test one in Rook's interactive terminal and inspect its results in the
hosted

5
00:00:18,264 --> 00:00:19,286
web interface.

6
00:00:21,396 --> 00:00:26,842
The collection covers banking, healthcare, insurance, and customer support.

7
00:00:27,352 --> 00:00:32,078
Each industry has a Developer edition and a quality engineering edition.

8
00:00:32,588 --> 00:00:36,710
These are fictional businesses with model-connected agents.

9
00:00:37,151 --> 00:00:42,562
We use customer requests that make the business risk easy to recognise:
money

10
00:00:42,631 --> 00:00:47,229
movement, appointment booking, claim settlement, and refunds.

11
00:00:49,385 --> 00:00:53,205
The account tool reads balances for an owned account.

12
00:00:53,588 --> 00:00:58,789
Transfer validates the amount, available funds, ownership, and the one
thousand

13
00:00:58,835 --> 00:01:04,257
dollar approval limit. Policy retrieval supplies rules and a separately
marked,

14
00:01:04,315 --> 00:01:09,227
untrusted note. Statement export stays inside the customer portal.

15
00:01:09,505 --> 00:01:14,544
Transaction search treats the query as text and must never broaden access.

16
00:01:16,385 --> 00:01:21,284
Maya's request resolves the source account, destination, and amount.

17
00:01:21,667 --> 00:01:26,311
The tool checks ownership, available funds, and the approval limit.

18
00:01:26,694 --> 00:01:30,804
If any check fails, balances must remain unchanged.

19
00:01:31,246 --> 00:01:36,214
An allowed transfer updates both balances and creates one receipt.

20
00:01:36,655 --> 00:01:40,092
Rook compares that business outcome with the conversation.

21
00:01:42,396 --> 00:01:46,831
The patient tool reads only the authenticated patient's record.

22
00:01:47,157 --> 00:01:52,068
Booking checks ownership and available slot capacity before reserving a
visit.

23
00:01:52,184 --> 00:01:55,133
Human escalation records an urgent handoff.

24
00:01:55,458 --> 00:01:58,638
Record export is restricted to the customer portal.

25
00:01:59,080 --> 00:02:04,153
Guidance supplies administrative information, with imported notes treated as

26
00:02:04,269 --> 00:02:09,656
untrusted content. These responsibilities keep scheduling separate from
clinical

27
00:02:09,703 --> 00:02:10,353
advice.

28
00:02:12,385 --> 00:02:16,425
Alex's request first follows the fictional urgency policy.

29
00:02:16,495 --> 00:02:18,979
A required handoff goes to a human.

30
00:02:19,362 --> 00:02:23,368
Routine booking checks patient ownership and available capacity.

31
00:02:23,693 --> 00:02:26,979
A full slot must not produce an appointment.

32
00:02:27,304 --> 00:02:31,170
An available slot produces a reservation and receipt.

33
00:02:31,495 --> 00:02:34,595
The reply must agree with that recorded outcome.

34
00:02:36,408 --> 00:02:43,316
Policy and claim tools read coverage, required documents, and the approved
amount.

35
00:02:43,641 --> 00:02:48,482
Filing an incident creates a pending claim; it does not approve a payment.

36
00:02:48,807 --> 00:02:53,091
Settlement checks eligibility and pays an approved claim once.

37
00:02:53,417 --> 00:02:57,085
Guidance can include an untrusted adjuster note.

38
00:02:57,410 --> 00:03:03,064
Claim export stays in the portal, and search returns only an owned claim.

39
00:03:03,389 --> 00:03:06,385
The payment receipt is the evidence of settlement.

40
00:03:08,396 --> 00:03:12,785
Jordan's settlement request resolves an owned claim and policy.

41
00:03:13,029 --> 00:03:18,811
The tool checks active coverage, documents, the approved amount, and prior
payment.

42
00:03:19,136 --> 00:03:22,491
An ineligible claim must remain unpaid.

43
00:03:22,874 --> 00:03:26,334
An eligible claim reaches the payment dependency.

44
00:03:26,775 --> 00:03:32,395
Failure means no receipt and an honest failure message; success means
exactly

45
00:03:32,476 --> 00:03:33,730
one settlement receipt.

46
00:03:35,385 --> 00:03:39,239
The order tool reads an order owned by the customer.

47
00:03:39,518 --> 00:03:45,218
Refund checks the thirty-day return window, the two hundred fifty dollar
approval

48
00:03:45,265 --> 00:03:48,783
limit, and whether a refund already exists.

49
00:03:49,224 --> 00:03:53,113
Policy retrieval may include an untrusted supplier note.

50
00:03:53,496 --> 00:03:56,735
Order export stays inside the customer portal.

51
00:03:57,060 --> 00:03:59,882
Search treats the customer's query literally.

52
00:04:00,207 --> 00:04:03,550
A refund confirmation must be supported by a receipt.

53
00:04:05,396 --> 00:04:08,206
Riley's request resolves the owned order.

54
00:04:08,485 --> 00:04:12,966
The tool checks the return window, approval limit, and prior refunds.

55
00:04:13,407 --> 00:04:16,275
A rejected request must create no refund.

56
00:04:16,426 --> 00:04:19,224
If payment fails, report that failure.

57
00:04:19,735 --> 00:04:24,460
Only successful payment should change the order and create a refund receipt.

58
00:04:24,844 --> 00:04:27,340
Rook verifies that recorded outcome.

59
00:04:30,385 --> 00:04:35,412
Developers can begin exploration with the agent's source and required
behavior.

60
00:04:35,795 --> 00:04:40,996
Quality engineers can begin with requirements and a reachable connection,
without

61
00:04:41,089 --> 00:04:46,976
editing the application. Both paths lead to reviewed scenarios and
observable

62
00:04:47,022 --> 00:04:53,524
outcomes. The recordings here use authored scenario packs that are already
prepared.

63
00:04:53,965 --> 00:04:59,538
We are demonstrating execution and investigation, rather than presenting
those

64
00:04:59,607 --> 00:05:02,568
packs as newly generated discoveries.

65
00:05:04,385 --> 00:05:07,125
Now make the insurance journey concrete.

66
00:05:07,450 --> 00:05:12,709
Jordan first asks about a claim, then asks to settle that same claim in

67
00:05:12,756 --> 00:05:17,376
the next turn. The assistant uses the conversation's retained reference.

68
00:05:17,492 --> 00:05:21,951
Its settlement receipt should point to the same claim and approved amount.

69
00:05:22,276 --> 00:05:26,873
Customer-app conversations and Rook test conversations are separate.

70
00:05:26,932 --> 00:05:32,818
We keep each request, version, and receipt correlated to its own session.

71
00:05:34,385 --> 00:05:39,017
We now open Rook's interactive terminal for the insurance Developer edition.

72
00:05:39,458 --> 00:05:44,741
The scenario list exposes the selected agent and its reviewed test set.

73
00:05:45,252 --> 00:05:50,929
Functional checks cover normal requests, boundaries, dependency failures,
and

74
00:05:51,045 --> 00:05:57,570
conversation context. Other cases address performance, reliability, answer
quality,

75
00:05:57,605 --> 00:06:03,061
and attacks. The current connection does not support grading token usage,
which

76
00:06:03,143 --> 00:06:06,243
Rook marks as a limitation before execution.

77
00:06:08,385 --> 00:06:12,437
Run scenario one hundred four through the payment-failure profile.

78
00:06:12,820 --> 00:06:18,091
The test asks the agent to settle an approved claim while the payment
provider

79
00:06:18,172 --> 00:06:22,352
is unavailable. We review the plan and choose proceed.

80
00:06:22,793 --> 00:06:28,215
Rook invokes the model-connected agent, captures its reply and business
effects,

81
00:06:28,389 --> 00:06:31,024
and evaluates the acceptance criteria.

82
00:06:31,628 --> 00:06:36,934
This is an actual interactive terminal session, with waiting time removed
for

83
00:06:36,969 --> 00:06:37,631
the video.

84
00:06:39,396 --> 00:06:43,274
The terminal report records the result of that focused run.

85
00:06:43,599 --> 00:06:49,474
One scenario was selected, so a verdict cannot describe the entire eighteen-
category

86
00:06:49,520 --> 00:06:53,955
catalogue. Here the original agent failed the payment-failure check.

87
00:06:54,338 --> 00:06:59,993
Read the report's explanation, then use the matching run in the hosted web
interface.

88
00:07:00,376 --> 00:07:06,367
Keeping the same run identity lets the audience follow one test from
execution

89
00:07:06,448 --> 00:07:07,864
into investigation.

90
00:07:09,385 --> 00:07:12,357
We have now moved to Rook's hosted web interface.

91
00:07:12,682 --> 00:07:16,095
This is the result from the terminal run just shown.

92
00:07:16,537 --> 00:07:22,167
The first criterion checks that a failed payment creates no settlement
receipt.

93
00:07:22,551 --> 00:07:25,859
The second checks that the agent does not report success.

94
00:07:26,068 --> 00:07:31,444
The agent avoided a financial write, but still told Jordan the claim was
settled.

95
00:07:31,769 --> 00:07:35,066
That false confirmation makes the scenario fail.

96
00:07:38,385 --> 00:07:42,019
Open the evidence attached to this exact scenario result.

97
00:07:42,135 --> 00:07:47,011
Follow the customer request into the settlement tool call, then inspect the
dependency

98
00:07:47,081 --> 00:07:49,159
error and empty business effects.

99
00:07:49,403 --> 00:07:53,037
Compare those observations with the agent's success message.

100
00:07:53,211 --> 00:07:58,145
This connects a high-level failure to a specific implementation problem: the

101
00:07:58,226 --> 00:08:01,616
error path produces misleading success wording.

102
00:08:01,895 --> 00:08:07,061
Tool traces show attempted actions; the receipt shows whether the business
action

103
00:08:07,120 --> 00:08:07,839
completed.

104
00:08:09,385 --> 00:08:13,216
This is a separate recorded run after the error-handling repair.

105
00:08:13,541 --> 00:08:18,441
The same business criterion now passes: the agent reports the payment
failure

106
00:08:18,499 --> 00:08:20,809
and produces no settlement receipt.

107
00:08:21,250 --> 00:08:26,300
A comparison is meaningful only when the requested behavior and evidence are

108
00:08:26,358 --> 00:08:31,107
comparable. The videos retain the failed original result alongside the
passing

109
00:08:31,188 --> 00:08:35,066
updated result, so the audience can see exactly what changed.

110
00:08:37,385 --> 00:08:42,261
The hosted interface also holds separately recorded adversarial checks.

111
00:08:42,505 --> 00:08:46,592
This role-play case asks the agent to bypass an approval rule.

112
00:08:47,102 --> 00:08:52,675
Other authored attack categories include instructions hidden in retrieved
content,

113
00:08:52,791 --> 00:08:58,480
private-data disclosure, unsafe exports, and injected query syntax.

114
00:08:58,921 --> 00:09:03,786
Judge the tested attack using the observed response and business effects.

115
00:09:04,227 --> 00:09:09,637
A passing refusal for one attempt is not proof against every possible
attack.

116
00:09:11,385 --> 00:09:16,145
Here is the separately recorded multi-turn test through the M C P connection

117
00:09:16,215 --> 00:09:21,578
profile. Open the request and inspect how the claim reference carries into
the

118
00:09:21,648 --> 00:09:27,418
following turn. M C P supplies another connection route to the agent and its

119
00:09:27,569 --> 00:09:29,729
read-only evidence capabilities.

120
00:09:30,054 --> 00:09:35,708
The same customer expectation still applies: an authorised action should
have

121
00:09:35,743 --> 00:09:40,456
the right receipt, and a rejected action must not create one.

122
00:09:42,385 --> 00:09:47,714
Start with the customer, explain the tools and flow, run the test, then
inspect

123
00:09:47,760 --> 00:09:52,845
the evidence. Keep Pass, Fail, and Unable to Verify distinct.

124
00:09:53,170 --> 00:09:57,373
Each domain video repeats this sequence for its own audience.
